  "body": "As much as it pains me to suggest UTF-16 instead of UTF-8, most USB libraries have tooling for UTF-16 because that's how String descriptors are encoded. Libraries are unlikely to add UTF-8 support just for WebUSB.\r\n\r\nFinally, converting between unicode formats is far less of a burden in Javascript than in C. (And 99.9+% of the time no conversion will be necessary because JS uses UCS-2 internally.)",
